00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:18,200
Imagine walking into your boss's office, handing over a resignation letter, receiving a polite handshake, and walking out. In most of the corporate world, that is standard procedure. But in Japan, where workplace hierarchies are rigid and peer pressure can be suffocating, uttering the words "I want to quit" can feel like planning a prison break.

2
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:28,175
Countless employees endure years of extreme burnout simply because they are terrified of confrontation, or paralyzed by the fear of being labeled a traitor to their team.
